  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>First step of the reaction is dehydrohalogenation and then ozonolysis.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0158_c42cf4e0bd92.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 288px;\" /></p><p>The dehydrohalogenation of alkyl halides, another &szlig; elimination reaction, involves the loss of a hydrogen and a halide from an alkyl halide (RX). Dehydrohalogenation is normally accomplished by reacting the alkyl halide with a strong base, such as sodium ethoxide.</p>"
